    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        What actually tightens the appearance of pores
    </h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Although you cannot change your genetic pore baseline, you can treat the underlying factors that stretch them. Refinement comes down to three things: clearing internal clogs, regulating oil output, and protecting the collagen around the pore from sun damage.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        First, oil-soluble salicylic acid dissolves the blend of sebum and dead cells trapped inside the follicle canal, allowing pore walls to relax back to their resting diameter. Simultaneously, topical niacinamide regulates sebum excretion rates. Clinical studies demonstrate that 2% niacinamide significantly reduces facial sebum levels over two to four weeks, preventing oil from pooling in the follicle.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16766489/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color:#B87330;text-decoration:none;">3</a></sup>
    </p>
    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Second, a serum can help with visible pores directly. In the clinical trial for <a href="/products/dark-spots-pore-control-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Dark Spots, Pore Control Serum</a> conducted on 36 Indian women aged 24 to 44, visible pore area was reduced by 19.3% at four weeks with twice-daily use (results may vary). The formula pairs niacinamide with six peptides, while five ceramides and cholesterol support the moisture barrier.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Finally, daily broad-spectrum sunscreen is crucial. Ultraviolet rays degrade collagen around the pore funnel, accelerating sagging and widening the opening. Daily sun protection preserves the firmness required to keep pores tight.<sup><a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/face/treat-large-pores" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color:#B87330;text-decoration:none;">4</a></sup>
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Skincare ingredients compared for pore care
    </h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Different actives address different causes of enlarged pores. Matching the ingredient to your primary concern delivers visible refinement without stressing your skin barrier.
    </p>

